# Consolidated .gitignore for the entire project (TasteTier)
#
# This file combines ignore rules from both the .idea and base directories.
# Having one top-level .gitignore makes it easier to manage and ensures consistency
# across the project. The extra .gitignore files (in .idea and base) are redundant and
# should be deleted once this file is in place.
#
# NOTE: If you encounter errors like:
# "error: Your local changes to the following files would be overwritten by checkout:
#         .idea/gradle.xml
#         .idea/misc.xml"
# It means these files have been previously committed and are being tracked.
# They are IDE-specific settings and should not be version controlled.
# To fix this, run:
#   git rm --cached .idea/gradle.xml .idea/misc.xml
# and then commit the changes.
#
# This will ensure local changes to these files do not interfere with branch operations.

### IntelliJ IDEA ###
# Ignore the entire IntelliJ IDEA project folder and its generated files.
# This prevents IDE-specific settings (which vary per user) from being committed.
.idea/
*.iml
*.iws
out/
!out/.gitkeep

### Cursor IDE ###
.cursor/

